pi-roamgate-docker — third-party attributions
===============================================

This repository packages three upstream projects into Docker images. It
redistributes each project's compiled/installed artifacts inside those
images (this is packaging, not merely "download at build time" — once an
image is built, it contains and redistributes the upstream binary/package).

1. herdr
   - Source: https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr
   - Version pinned: v0.9.1
   - License: Apache License 2.0
   - License text bundled at: /usr/share/licenses/herdr/LICENSE (fetched
     from the pinned git tag at build time)
   - Note: there is no upstream root NOTICE file to propagate for this
     project as of v0.9.1.

2. roamgate
   - Source: https://github.com/powerfooI/roamgate
   - Version pinned: v0.7.8
   - License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Arthur
   - License text bundled at: /usr/share/licenses/roamgate/LICENSE (fetched
     from the pinned git tag at build time)
   - Bundled fonts and brand assets in roamgate's own embedded web UI retain
     their original terms per roamgate's own THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md; not
     reproduced here.

3. pi (pi coding agent)
   - Package: @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent (npm) — note the package
     scope uses a HYPHEN, "earendil-works", not a dot.
   - Version pinned: 0.87.0
   - License: MIT
   - License text bundled at: /usr/share/licenses/pi/LICENSE (copied from
     the installed npm package tree at build time)

4. gh (GitHub CLI) and kubectl
   - Installed as binaries only (no credential wiring in this pass; see
     README.md "Known limitations"). gh is MIT-licensed; kubectl is
     Apache-2.0. See /usr/share/licenses/gh/LICENSE and
     /usr/share/licenses/kubectl/NOTE inside the built images.

Out of scope for this pass
---------------------------
Published images would additionally redistribute each project's own
dependencies — for example herdr vendors libghostty-vt and portable-pty
(each under their own licenses), and pi has its own npm dependency tree. A
full third-party dependency license inventory / SBOM has NOT been produced
in this pass and should be generated before any registry publication of
these images.

The packaging work itself (Dockerfiles, compose.yaml, install/entrypoint
scripts, documentation) is licensed MIT — see LICENSE.
